// ModelSwapper cvars.

// CONFIG VERSION. Bumped whenever a shipped DEFAULT changes, so an existing
// ini picks the change up instead of silently overriding it -- an archived
// server cvar always beats this file. See RS_ForeignModelHandler.MigrateConfig,
// which applies the change once and stamps this.
//
//   0 -- never migrated. A fresh install starts here, already holds the
//        current defaults from below, and is stamped on first load.
//   1 -- rs_foreignmodels_byfamily defaults off.
server int rs_fm_cfgver = 0;

server bool rs_foreignmodels         = true;   // master switch
server bool rs_foreignmodels_dump    = false;  // dump the scan to console
server bool rs_foreignmodels_showall = false;  // include weapons with no slot binding

// (rs_foreignmodels_natural and rs_fm_learned are gone: the remap engine
// reads timing off the weapon's own state table every tic, so there is
// no learned timing to store and no "natural rate" distinct from theirs.
// A stale archived copy in an old ini is ignored harmlessly.)

// The player's own model choices, packed as class:archetype:pick1:pick2;...
// Written every time a pick changes. Keyed on class name only -- no notion
// of "which mod" anywhere -- which is what makes this work as a per-mod
// profile with nothing tracking which mod is loaded: only one mod's classes
// exist in the world at a time. Clear it with the menu.
server string rs_fm_picks = "";

// Hitscan -> projectile conversion. Off by default, and the only setting
// here that changes how the loaded mod plays rather than how it looks.
server bool rs_fm_ballistic       = false;  // player hitscans become travelling rounds
// 300, not 90, for two reasons that happen to agree.
//
// GunBonsai infers whether a weapon is a hitscan or a projectile weapon from
// the speed of what it fires, and counts anything at 300 map units per tic or
// faster as a hitscan -- a threshold it added for mods that simulate bullets
// with fast projectiles, which is exactly what this is. Below it, every
// converted shotgun and rifle is filed as a projectile weapon and offered the
// wrong upgrade tree. It also credits XP to the weapon held when the round
// LANDS, so a shorter flight time is a smaller window to fire, swap, and have
// the XP go to the wrong gun.
//
// It is also the fastest the trail can draw at full density: one bit per 12
// units, 24 per tic, so 300 units of travel is 25 requested against 24 allowed.
// Faster than this and the streak starts to gap.
server int  rs_fm_ballistic_speed = 300;    // map units per tic, clamped 10-400

// WHICH ROUND YOU SEE. Behaviour is identical across all five -- same
// travel time, same range cutoff, same damage, same impact puff handed
// back to the mod. Only the look differs.
//
//   1  plain    -- a round in flight, nothing behind it (default)
//   2  zdoom    -- small clean dot, no trail
//   3  lpuf     -- glowing streak, tapers as it fades
//   4  dpuf     -- two-frame round, four bouncing sparks on impact
//   5  layered  -- six-particle wake; the densest, and the only one that
//                  stays continuous at 300 units/tic
//
// Types 2-5 are HF's VR_ZDoomBullet, VR_LPUFBullet, VR_DPUFBullet and
// HF_LayeredBullet. Its sprites are not ours to ship (its own
// ASSET_PROVENANCE.md files LPUF and DPUF as unresolved rips), so all
// four draw on the stock PUFF instead.
server int rs_fm_ballistic_type = 1;   // clamped 1-5

// Bullet Time X compensation. Inert unless that mod is loaded alongside.
// 0.0 = player as slow as the monsters, 1.0 = normal player movement speed
// -- their own player-divisor cvar has no faster setting than that, so 1.0
// is the true ceiling, not a compromise. Default 0.0 because Bullet Time X
// itself ships with the player divisor equal to the world divisor -- 0.0 IS
// their own out-of-the-box behavior, so enabling this changes nothing until
// the slider actually moves.
server bool   rs_fm_bt       = false;
server float  rs_fm_bt_scale = 0.0;
// Their player-movement divisors as they were before we touched them,
// packed "normal:dodge:berserk:berserkdodge". Kept in a cvar so quitting
// with compensation on cannot strand their settings overwritten.
server string rs_fm_bt_base  = "";

// Extra distance from the grip to the muzzle, on top of the per-family
// figure. The engine has no muzzle concept -- shots start at the hand.
server int rs_fm_muzzle = 0;   // map units, clamped -20..80

// Collapse the picker to ONE ROW PER FAMILY -- one shotgun row, one smg row.
//
// OFF by default. The picker exists to show the weapons the scan actually
// found, by name, and let you put a model on each one. A row labelled
// "all shotgun" answers a question nobody asked first.
//
// Turn it ON when a mod's class count makes that unworkable: Brutal Doom 22
// shows 85 rows, DoomRL Arsenal about 150, and across the test corpus there
// are 934 weapon classes of which only 276 even declare a slot. Most of
// those rows are the same gun in a different mode -- BrutalPistol,
// DualPistols and PuristPistol are all your pistol -- and one row per
// family is the escape hatch for exactly that case.
server bool rs_foreignmodels_byfamily = false;

// Show only weapons you are CARRYING. The cheapest honest filter there is:
// a mod can invent classes without limit, but you only ever hold the ones
// your player class was given. Guncaster and Trailblazer name their weapons
// Brimstone and Bitchmaker -- no token list will ever classify those, and no
// filter built on names will ever shorten that menu. Your inventory answers
// both questions without asking the mod anything.
//
// Off by default: a player who wants to dress a gun before finding it should
// meet the whole list first.
server bool rs_foreignmodels_carried = false;

// Offer models even when a weapon already has one of its own.
//
// ON by default, because the flag we can read cannot answer the question we
// actually have. Actor.hasmodel means "this class has a model bound to SOME
// sprite" -- it says nothing about WHICH. A mod that models its dropped
// pickup and leaves the first-person view as flat sprites reads identically
// to one that ships full HUD models.
//
// Project Brutality is exactly that mod. Its MODELDEF binds sprite VIFL and
// its Spawn state runs A_PBVPFramework -- the pickup lying on the floor. Its
// Fire states use R0F8 and have no model at all. hasmodel came back true, we
// stood down, and we withheld models from the weapons that most needed them.
//
// Pickup models are common; first-person weapon models are rare -- a mod
// that had them would not need this one. So offering is the right default.
// Turn this off to leave any modelled weapon alone.
server bool rs_foreignmodels_replaceown = true;

// THE WHEEL BRIDGE -- for RS_WeaponWheel's model-picker page, or any other
// reflection-based reader. No compile-time dependency in either direction:
// they find these two by NAME and write an int, we read and clear it once
// per tic (RS_ForeignModelHandler.RefreshBridge, called from WorldTick).
// +1/-1 cycles that hand's pick by one entry; 0 is "nothing pending".
//
// nosave, because a command flag has no business surviving to the next
// session -- WorldTick clears it same-tick, so anything saved would only
// ever be a stray nonzero from a crash mid-tic.
user nosave int rs_fm_bridge_cmd_main = 0;
user nosave int rs_fm_bridge_cmd_off  = 0;
